{"id": "DfKjHakx5Z_", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Parshurama won his first war with NO weapons. Before the axe, before the name, there was just a young RAMA and his bare hands. 🪓🔱\n\nRama, son of the sage Jamadagni, prayed to Shiva for one thing: weapons. Shiva's answer: \"I will give them to you when you are pure. These weapons burn anyone who is unfit.\"\n\nSo he kept praying, for years. Shiva told the gods, \"This Rama is devoted to me.\"\n\nThen the demons rose against the gods, and Shiva sent Rama to fight them. \"But Lord, I have no weapons!\" \"Go. You will win.\"\n\nHe beat them with his bare hands, with blows like Indra's thunderbolt. He came back wounded, and one touch of Shiva healed him. Then came Shiva's gifts: divine weapons… and one axe.\n\nPARASHU means axe. Rama + Parashu = PARSHURAMA. 🙏\n\n📖 Sources: Mahabharata, Karna Parva 8.24 (Critical Edition) and Anushasana Parva 13.18, where Parshurama himself says Shiva gave him the axe.\n\nThis is Part 2 of our Parshurama series. Every part stands on its own, so start anywhere!\n\n📚 The Navadurga Set, kids' picture books on the nine forms of Maa Durga, is out now at rishikatha.com (link in bio).\n\n💬 Comment \"HAR HAR MAHADEV\" 🔱\n🔁 Share it with someone who didn't know where his name comes from!\n📌 Save it for story time.\n\n#parshurama #parashurama #harharmahadev #mahadev #shiva #vishnuavatar #dashavatar #mahabharata #hindumythology #sanatandharma #indianmythology #hindustories #storiesforkids #rishikatha #jaiparshuram", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1793462921, "like_count": 5290, "comment_count": 69, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1692616795531178a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 48.938, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr22-2.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQP62